WEBVTT

00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:06.884
"Spiders flee before it."

00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:08.538
It all fits.

00:00:08.538 --> 00:00:11.019
But how's the basilisk
been getting around?

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:13.761
A dirty, great snake,
someone would have seen it.

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:15.980
Hermione's answered
that too.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.810
Pipes?
It's using the plumbing.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.246
Remember
what Aragog said

00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:24.380
about that girl
50 years ago?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.903
She died in a bathroom?

00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:28.384
What if she never left?

00:00:28.384 --> 00:00:31.169
Moaning Myrtle.

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:33.476
PROFESSOR MCGONAGALL:
All students are to return

00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:35.043
to their house dormitories
at once.

00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:36.653
All teachers

00:00:36.653 --> 00:00:38.916
to the second floor corridor
immediately.

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:45.923
As you can see,

00:00:45.923 --> 00:00:50.536
the Heir of Slytherin
has left another message.

00:00:50.536 --> 00:00:52.930
Our worst fear
has been realized.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.063
A student has been taken
by the monster

00:00:55.063 --> 00:00:56.847
into the Chamber itself.

00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.285
The students must be sent home.

00:01:00.285 --> 00:01:02.897
I'm afraid
this is the end of Hogwarts.

00:01:06.074 --> 00:01:08.554
So sorry. Dozed off.
What have I missed?

00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:11.079
A girl has been snatched
by the monster, Lockhart.

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:13.429
Your moment
has come at last.

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:14.996
My...moment?

00:01:14.996 --> 00:01:16.606
Weren't you saying
just last night

00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:18.216
that you've
known all along

00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:19.652
where the entrance to
the Chamber of Secrets is?

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.700
That's settled.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.660
We'll leave you to deal
with the monster, Gilderoy.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.880
Your skills, after all,
are legend.

00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:33.492
Very well.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:37.279
Uh, I'll just be in my office
getting...

00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:39.585
Getting ready.

00:01:41.674 --> 00:01:44.416
Who is it that
the monster's taken, Minerva?

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:47.289
Ginny Weasley.

00:01:58.387 --> 00:02:01.781
"Her skeleton will lie
in the chamber forever."

00:02:05.437 --> 00:02:06.874
Ginny...

00:02:09.746 --> 00:02:11.356
Lockhart may be useless,

00:02:11.356 --> 00:02:13.445
but he's going to try
and get into the Chamber.

00:02:13.445 --> 00:02:16.013
At least we can tell him
what we know!

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.974
Professor, we have
some information for you.

00:02:21.845 --> 00:02:23.325
Are you going
somewhere?

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:25.022
Uh, well, yes. Um...

00:02:25.022 --> 00:02:26.458
Urgent call.
Unavoidable, uh...

00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:27.503
Got to go.

00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:28.504
What about my sister?

00:02:28.504 --> 00:02:30.593
Well...um...

00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:32.725
As to that,
most unfortunate.

00:02:32.725 --> 00:02:34.945
No one regrets
more than I.

00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:37.252
You're the Defense
Against the Dark Arts teacher.

00:02:37.252 --> 00:02:38.470
You can't go now.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.168
Well, I must say,
when I took the job,

00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:42.213
there was nothing
in the job description about--

00:02:42.213 --> 00:02:43.693
You're running away?

00:02:43.693 --> 00:02:45.347
After all that stuff
you did in your books?

00:02:45.347 --> 00:02:46.522
Books can be misleading.

00:02:46.522 --> 00:02:47.740
You wrote them!

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.133
My dear boy,
do use your common sense!

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:50.830
My books wouldn't have sold
half as well

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.224
if people didn't think
I'd done all those things!

00:02:53.224 --> 00:02:55.748
You're a fraud.

00:02:55.748 --> 00:02:58.926
You've been taking credit for
what other wizards have done.

00:02:58.926 --> 00:03:00.492
Is there anything
you can do?

00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:02.799
Yes. Now you mention it.

00:03:02.799 --> 00:03:05.149
I'm rather gifted
with memory charms.

00:03:05.149 --> 00:03:06.498
Otherwise, you see,

00:03:06.498 --> 00:03:08.544
all those wizards
would have gone blabbing,

00:03:08.544 --> 00:03:10.763
and I'd never have sold
another book.

00:03:10.763 --> 00:03:13.157
In fact, uh...

00:03:13.157 --> 00:03:17.335
I'm going to have to do
the same to you.

00:03:17.335 --> 00:03:20.512
Don't even think about it.

00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:32.785
Oh, who's there?

00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:35.092
Oh!

00:03:35.092 --> 00:03:37.747
Hello, Harry.

00:03:37.747 --> 00:03:39.575
What do you want?

00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:43.405
To ask you
how you died.

00:03:43.405 --> 00:03:48.714
Oh, it was dreadful.

00:03:48.714 --> 00:03:52.718
It happened right here
in this very cubicle.

00:03:52.718 --> 00:03:56.244
I'd hidden because Olive Hornby
was teasing me about my glasses.

00:03:56.244 --> 00:03:57.636
I was crying...

00:03:57.636 --> 00:04:01.249
and then I heard
somebody come in.

00:04:01.249 --> 00:04:02.772
Who was it, Myrtle?

00:04:02.772 --> 00:04:05.601
I don't know.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:08.865
I was distraught!

00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:10.867
But they said
something funny,

00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:12.695
a kind of
made-up language,

00:04:12.695 --> 00:04:14.784
and I realized
it was a boy speaking,

00:04:14.784 --> 00:04:18.353
so I unlocked the door
to tell him to go away,

00:04:18.353 --> 00:04:20.529
and...

00:04:20.529 --> 00:04:22.096
I died.

00:04:22.096 --> 00:04:25.142
Just like that? How?

00:04:25.142 --> 00:04:30.278
I just remember seeing a pair
of great, big, yellow eyes...

00:04:30.278 --> 00:04:33.933
over there by that sink.

00:04:58.349 --> 00:05:01.831
This is it.

00:05:01.831 --> 00:05:04.094
This is it, Ron.

00:05:04.094 --> 00:05:06.575
I think this is the entrance
to the Chamber of Secrets.

00:05:08.794 --> 00:05:10.796
Say something.

00:05:10.796 --> 00:05:13.016
Harry, say something
in Parseltongue.

00:05:22.243 --> 00:05:26.203
[SPEAKS PARSELTONGUE]

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.641
[RUMBLING]

00:06:04.894 --> 00:06:06.548
Excellent, Harry.
Ah, good work.

00:06:06.548 --> 00:06:08.071
Well, then, I'll just be...

00:06:08.071 --> 00:06:09.986
There's no need for me to stay.

00:06:11.596 --> 00:06:13.207
Oh, yes, there is.

00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:14.208
[LOCKHART YELLS]

00:06:15.861 --> 00:06:17.211
You first.

00:06:17.211 --> 00:06:18.908
Now, boys, what good will it do?

00:06:18.908 --> 00:06:20.431
Better you than us.

00:06:20.431 --> 00:06:23.173
Um, but...
Obviously. Yes.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.137
Sure you don't want
to test it first?

00:06:30.137 --> 00:06:32.095
[YELLING]

00:06:35.359 --> 00:06:36.317
[CRASH]

00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:41.757
It's really
quite filthy down here.

00:06:41.757 --> 00:06:44.586
All right. Let's go.

00:06:44.586 --> 00:06:46.631
Oh, Harry?

00:06:46.631 --> 00:06:48.677
If you die down there,

00:06:48.677 --> 00:06:51.897
you're welcome
to share my toilet.

00:06:53.421 --> 00:06:57.599
Uh... Thanks, Myrtle.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.561
[HARRY & RON YELLING]

